If $k=2$, numbers are $10, \dots, 19$ (MSD 1, others < 1 i.e. 0), $20, \dots, 29$ (MSD 2, others < 2 i.e. 0, 1), etc.
For $x=1$, others $\in \{0\}$, so 1 number: 10.
For $x=2$, others $\in \{0, 1\}$, so 2 numbers: 20, 21.
For $x=9$, others $\in \{0, \dots, 8\}$, so 9 numbers: 90, ..., 98.
Total for $k=2$ is $\sum_{x=1}^9 x = 45$.
